Kind: ablation
Issue: #598
Takes out: the HPET passing over its FSB route while interrupts are remapped -- it composes the message in compatibility format again.  On QEMU the tick still runs, because QEMU's HPET writes the message past the IOMMU; on hardware the engine would refuse it and the tick would stop.  So what is caught here is the choice, said on the start line
Run: --iommu intel --entry 35 900 -smp 1 -global hpet.msi=on
Expect: clock_event: hpet: comparator [0-9]+ of [0-9]+, one-shot, 32 bits, FSB message to cpu

diff --git a/uros/src/mach_kernel/x86_64/time/hpet_event.c b/uros/src/mach_kernel/x86_64/time/hpet_event.c
index 72d61f61..8b8bc5ca 100644
--- a/uros/src/mach_kernel/x86_64/time/hpet_event.c
+++ b/uros/src/mach_kernel/x86_64/time/hpet_event.c
@@ -220,10 +220,6 @@ static int choose_route(unsigned *which, uint32_t *cap0)
 			 * be checked on hardware (#595).  The I/O APIC's pin
 			 * below is remapped like any other.
 			 */
-			if (iommu_interrupts_remapped()) {
-				fsb_passed_over = 1;
-				continue;
-			}
 			*which = n;
 			return ROUTE_FSB;
 		}
